WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.220
a book like he’s preparing to tell a story.]

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:04.740
Welcome, dear viewers, to another Tale of
excitement and intrigue from the archives

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.080
of the SCP Foundation.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.080
Today, we’re covering a peculiar story,
titled “Foundation Facilities and How to

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.130
Loot Them”.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:19.160
Our story opens on Shock, a member of SCP-4799,
frantically running for her life.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.980
SCP-4799, in case you aren’t already aware,
is a group of smugglers also known by the

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.660
name Mariachi’s Merchants.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.119
Now the Merchants aren’t your average, everyday
under-the-table traders mind you, this group

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:33.770
is capable of trans-universal travel.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.160
Stealing advanced technology from other universes,
members of Mariachi’s Merchants will then

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.680
sell these devices to turn a profit.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.960
Each of these members, of which there are
believed to be seven, originally comes from

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.620
a separate universe outside of our own.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:48.620
And Shock?

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.270
She’s one of their best.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:55.140
Blaster in her hand, Shock ran down the corridor,
stopping at a T-shaped intersection, frantically

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.680
trying to decide which way to turn next.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.810
The energy weapon in her hand was still warm
to the touch; she’d only just fired it,

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:06.060
down to its last twelve shots, thirteen if
she was lucky.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:11.110
There was only meant to be one life form nearby,
the only other living thing in a two-kilometer

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.800
radius, but Shock had quickly learned that
she was far from alone.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:22.070
Two… things wearing lab coats, things that
had perhaps once been human beings, were shambling

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.909
their way closer and closer to her.

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:28.000
The nearest door was locked, protected by
a keypad, but there was no time to hack her

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.340
way inside.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.650
Letting out a growl, Shock turned and opened
fire on her pursuers, the pair of creatures

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:39.020
that hadn’t registered as life forms, but
were still, inexplicably alive.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:43.299
Energy bolts spat from her blaster, disintegrating
them both in an instant.

00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:48.010
Turning her focus to the nearby door, Shock
pushed a thin black device into the key card

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:51.250
slot, connected to a thin screen that controlled
it.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:55.110
She grumbled about how what had seemed like
a simple scavenging mission had gone south

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:56.290
so quickly.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:00.810
The planet appeared to be dead, at least from
the perspective of the Mariachi’s Merchants’

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:01.930
ship in orbit.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.610
What was the worst that could have happened?

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:07.700
Turns out losing communication with her crew
for one, they’d been radio silent after

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.920
the ship was reportedly fired upon.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.280
The Merchants had promised to come back for
Shock once they’d shaken off whoever was

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.410
shooting at them.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:19.349
The facility she was trying to scavenge had
once belonged to the SCP Foundation, presumably

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:22.840
a long time ago, codenamed Site 101.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:26.510
Built under a spacecraft launch compound,
it should have been a goldmine filled with

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.819
all sorts of valuable technology.

00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:32.750
But so far, it didn’t seem like there was
anything left in the facility that justified

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.310
the dangerous trip.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:38.840
The keypad flashed green as the door unlocked,
Shock collecting up her hacking device as

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:43.010
the door opened… and one of the creatures
appeared on the other side.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:47.610
Reacting with incredible speed, Shock blasted
the creature into dust, cursing at its body

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:50.099
as it disintegrated atom by atom.

00:02:50.099 --> 00:02:55.030
What were these things, and why did the Merchants’
sensors not read them as life forms?

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:59.320
She pushed the question to the back of her
mind, there was a time and place to contemplate

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.940
what could be classified as “alive”, and
this was neither.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:07.250
Hurtling down the newly-opened corridor, Shock
headed towards an open office door.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:11.490
Hiding as quietly as possible in the office,
making sure the door was secure enough that

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:16.330
those horrors outside wouldn’t follow her,
Shock took a moment to calm herself.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:20.980
She sat herself down on a leather chair in
front of the dark wood desk that filled most

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.740
of the space in the office.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:27.860
It had belonged to one Doctor Dwyer, according
to the computer that stood atop the desk,

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:32.709
which Shock began to hack into, once again
using her key card cracking device.

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:37.010
After about a half an hour of working through
some very sophisticated security software,

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:40.530
she eventually managed to force her way into
the computer and started clicking through

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.730
its files.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:45.590
The first thing she uncovered in a folder
that was conveniently labeled ‘Important’

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:50.410
was an email from the O5 command to the director
of this abandoned, former Foundation site,

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:53.240
along with other high-ranking members of personnel.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.959
The subject simply read’ Farewell’.

00:03:55.959 --> 00:04:00.459
In the email, O5-7 mentioned that the last
of a number of escape ships had successfully

00:04:00.459 --> 00:04:04.040
launched from Site 101 and arrived at colony
stations.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:08.310
It seemed that some kind of war was imminent
and would ravage the entire Earth, leaving

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.450
nothing behind.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:15.510
So, in their infinite wisdom, the SCP Foundation
had been using its vast resources to evacuate

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:16.760
its personnel off-world.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:21.989
Meanwhile, the personnel of Site 101 would
stay at their posts, perhaps to repopulate

00:04:21.989 --> 00:04:25.639
or rebuild the Earth after the impending war
had passed.

00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:31.550
That email had been sent in the year 2217,
a whole eighteen years before Shock had arrived

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.780
at this facility hoping to raid it.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:37.960
The next email in the folder was headed with
the word “Intruder”, sent just under a

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.290
month before.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:44.620
A pair of Foundation security personnel, Officers
Sanchez and Metje, had happened across a breach

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.500
to the ventilation system.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:51.490
According to their reports, it looked as if
someone or something had forced its way in

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.680
with some kind of metal implement.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:59.160
Shortly after, a third officer, Officer Peterson,
failed to respond to a radio check, seemingly

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.759
going missing.

00:05:00.759 --> 00:05:05.210
Security had been advised to travel in groups
and to engage any unknown entity with lethal

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:06.210
force.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:11.449
Something had made its way into the facility,
and it had arrived just before Shock did.

00:05:11.449 --> 00:05:16.650
Uneasy, still not sure what had happened here,
the dimension-hopping scavenger read on.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:20.960
The third and final email entry had been sent
the day after the last.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.540
This time, security had a better idea of what
they were up against.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:28.560
Surveillance footage from within the facility
had revealed the intruder to be none other

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.110
than SCP-049.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:35.759
It had claimed the lives of multiple security
officers, with two of them confirmed to have

00:05:35.759 --> 00:05:39.350
become instances of SCP-049-2.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:45.300
Being from a different universe, however,
Shock had no idea what an SCP-049 was, nor

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.100
did she like the idea of being trapped with
one.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:52.900
Now in case you, like Shock, haven’t heard
of the infamous Plague Doctor, then here’s

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:56.509
a brief bit of context on SCP-049.

00:05:56.509 --> 00:06:02.639
A tall figure, shrouded in long black robes,
a hood over his head with only a white, beaked

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:05.310
mask protruding from underneath.

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:09.889
These aren’t just parts of his attire though,
the SCP Foundation discovered that all of

00:06:09.889 --> 00:06:16.300
the pieces of SCP-049’s outfit are parts
of his physical body, made out of muscle and

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.300
bone.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:21.350
The Plague Doctor’s primary goal is to find
those he deems to be infected with something

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:23.810
he refers to as “the pestilence.”

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:27.949
If he ever senses this affliction, he will
attempt to make direct skin contact with the

00:06:27.949 --> 00:06:30.050
person carrying it.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:35.199
SCP-049’s touch is lethal, killing anyone
who comes into contact with him in a matter

00:06:35.199 --> 00:06:36.360
of minutes.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:40.490
You might think that’s all the Plague Doctor
does, goes from person to person, killing

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:41.639
them via touch.

00:06:41.639 --> 00:06:43.860
But you would be wrong.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:48.860
Once he has killed a victim, SCP-049 then
begins performing a crude, outdated form of

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:50.920
surgery on their corpse.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:55.410
Using equipment he produces from his mysterious
medical bag, he injects a number of unknown

00:06:55.410 --> 00:07:00.099
chemicals into a person’s carcass, eventually
turning them into an instance of SCP-049-2

00:07:00.099 --> 00:07:04.580
- In other words, a zombie.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:09.910
And that’s exactly what it had done to at
least two of the Site 101 security officers.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:14.560
When Shock delved further into the computer,
examining some security footage, not only

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:19.410
did she watch a monstrosity in a shredded
security uniform shambling through a corridor,

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.569
but there was something else following it.

00:07:21.569 --> 00:07:27.290
A figure, completely clad in black robes,
its face shrouded behind an eerie, beaked

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:28.389
mask.

00:07:28.389 --> 00:07:32.760
Shock decided her best course of action was
to find out as much as she could about SCP-049,

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:37.710
then use the facility’s security cameras
to figure out the quickest route to find any

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:41.580
propulsion tech that the Foundation might
have left lying around.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:47.199
She familiarized herself with the Foundation’s
extensive file on SCP-049, learning what the

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:51.789
Plague Doctor could do; the part Shock found
to be particularly unsettling was knowing

00:07:51.789 --> 00:07:56.460
the entity could shut down an organism’s
biological functions whenever it made direct

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.200
skin contact.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.990
Best to try and avoid him, she told herself.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:06.050
Studying the camera feeds, Shock noticed the
SCP-049-2s, that had all been the former staff

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:10.580
of this facility, didn’t seem to move around
much unless provoked.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:14.830
All she had to do was make it through the
corridors to a door labeled “Propulsion

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:17.770
Testing” without the “dash twos” noticing
her.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:21.770
Sounds easy enough in theory, and it would
have been easier in practice if there weren’t

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:25.190
currently eight of the zombies standing in
her path to the testing room.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:29.450
With a tight grip around her blaster, Shock
bolted from the office, barrelling at full

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:31.020
sprint down the corridor.

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:35.559
She already knew from watching the cameras
that the first of the SCP-049-2s was around

00:08:35.559 --> 00:08:36.749
the nearest corner.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:41.560
Opening fire, she went speeding past its remains
as it turned into a little more than a smoldering

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:43.379
pile on the floor.

00:08:43.379 --> 00:08:46.860
Around the next corner were another two of
the creatures, dispatched as quickly as the

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.990
first with the bright blue crackle of the
energy weapon.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:56.190
So far, so good, but Shock was already anticipating
seeing a group of five SCP-049-2s huddled

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:59.480
together, the next obstacle in her way.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:03.949
Sure enough, she navigated her way through
the facility’s hallways towards them, making

00:09:03.949 --> 00:09:06.829
sure she had the element of surprise on her
side.

00:09:06.829 --> 00:09:11.279
She blasted the oncoming mob of zombies, screaming
as they were struck by the blue light of her

00:09:11.279 --> 00:09:15.019
blaster, only to vanish, vaporized forever.

00:09:15.019 --> 00:09:20.170
All except for the fifth and final SCP-049-2
instance.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:24.300
Shock had fired her fifth shot too soon, missing
the last of the creatures.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:28.450
She waited for it to close the distance between
them, hoping for a closer target, but the

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:30.769
monstrosity knocked the gun from her hands.

00:09:30.769 --> 00:09:33.230
They scuffled, Shock pulled a fusion bomb
from her bag.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:37.249
Wrapping the unstable energy cell in her coat,
she let the creature grab the makeshift bomb

00:09:37.249 --> 00:09:41.220
from her, picking up her weapon and running
as the bomb detonated.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:46.139
Exhausted, she reached the Propulsion Testing
room, injured after her fight with the “dash

00:09:46.139 --> 00:09:49.079
two”, Shock had hoped her troubles were
over.

00:09:49.079 --> 00:09:51.819
And for a moment, they certainly seemed to
be.

00:09:51.819 --> 00:09:56.110
She had stumbled across a motherload of tech,
modified reality anchors and all kinds of

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:58.559
equipment that would be perfect salvage.

00:09:58.559 --> 00:10:04.809
But then, from the shadows, something new
stepped forward: the Plague Doctor himself.

00:10:04.809 --> 00:10:08.980
Shock drew her blaster again and pulled the
trigger, but the weapon was spent, sparking

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:11.129
in her hands as it failed to fire.

00:10:11.129 --> 00:10:15.589
Frozen, she stared at SCP-049, and it stared
back.

00:10:15.589 --> 00:10:19.799
Lowering her weapon, Shock tried to calmly
introduce herself to the looming, cloaked

00:10:19.799 --> 00:10:20.799
anomaly.

00:10:20.799 --> 00:10:21.869
“I’m Shock.

00:10:21.869 --> 00:10:22.959
Nice to meet you…

00:10:22.959 --> 00:10:26.799
You're… or rather, these people called you
SCP forty-nine, right?

00:10:26.799 --> 00:10:30.170
You sure did a bang-up job of curing everyone
in here from the looks of things.”

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.139
For a moment, they talked.

00:10:32.139 --> 00:10:36.540
SCP-049 had heard the Foundation personnel
at Site 101 talking of being the last men

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:41.749
on Earth, and made its way into the facility
to “save them” as he put it, ridding them

00:10:41.749 --> 00:10:43.009
of “the Pestilence.”

00:10:43.009 --> 00:10:47.059
Shock explained that the rest of the planet’s
surface outside had been severely irradiated

00:10:47.059 --> 00:10:52.259
and that there was no one living up top anymore,
all while sneakily sliding pieces of expensive-looking

00:10:52.259 --> 00:10:54.680
tech into her bag.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:59.679
SCP-049 argued that there were still people
left on Earth, that Site 42 housed the very

00:10:59.679 --> 00:11:01.189
last remnants of humanity.

00:11:01.189 --> 00:11:06.100
But they had been untouched by disease, they
were pure.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:08.209
But Shock didn’t care one bit.

00:11:08.209 --> 00:11:12.999
Instead, she made a move nobody would have
expected, she offered the Plague Doctor a

00:11:12.999 --> 00:11:13.999
lift.

00:11:13.999 --> 00:11:17.329
The Mariachi’s Merchants would be coming
back for her soon, and their ship was able

00:11:17.329 --> 00:11:19.959
to take them anywhere in the multiverse.

00:11:19.959 --> 00:11:25.329
After pondering for a moment, SCP-049 asked
to be taken with them, to find where the rest

00:11:25.329 --> 00:11:28.929
of the sick were, unwilling to accept his
work was done.

00:11:28.929 --> 00:11:33.360
“As long as you agree to keep your hands
to yourself,” Shock told him, as a grey

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:37.049
orb appeared in the room, hovering above the
floor, without touching the ceiling.

00:11:37.049 --> 00:11:39.459
It was time to leave.

00:11:39.459 --> 00:11:45.439
Now go check out “SCP-049 - the Plague Doctor
Captured” and “SCP-049 - What Actually

00:11:45.439 --> 00:11:46.679
is the Pestilence?

00:11:46.679 --> 00:11:50.899
The Plague Doctor Questions and Theories”
for more videos that definitely won’t give

00:11:50.899 --> 00:11:52.449
you The Pestilence!

00:11:52.449 --> 00:11:53.810
Seriously, we promise!

